          {
            "readme_said": "curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSLf https://termscp.rs/install.sh | sh",
            "actually_needed": "On Debian the script downloads the .deb and installs it with sudo apt/dpkg, which needs root. Without root, download termscp_1.2.2-1_amd64.deb from the GitHub release, extract it with dpkg-deb -x and copy usr/bin/termscp onto PATH. The binary is static, so it runs as is.",
